{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Midianite traders.</b> Owners of the Ishmaelite camels' trade:" "<b>And they sold Joseph to the Ishmaelites.</b> They conducted the sale through the Midianite traders on behalf of the Ishmaelites, for they did not wish to deal directly with the traders, lest they be recognized when the traders sometimes stayed in towns to sell. Instead, they dealt with the camel-owners, who do not linger in towns but merely pass through them in transit, and through them they executed the sale. But the buyers were the Midianite traders, as it says: <b>And the Medanites sold him to Egypt</b>. So too it happened to our fathers in the Second Temple: some of them sold some of their brethren into the hand of the Romans — especially when the Hasmonean kings made war against each other, enslaving Israel to the Romans and bringing this exile upon us — just as the matter of Joseph's sale unfolded, leading to our fathers' descent into Egypt, as the Sages of blessed memory stated (Shabbat 10a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:45.040150141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}